<a href="https://www.waze.com">Waze</a> and <a href="https://www.garmin.com/en-US/">Garmin</a> have announced the launch of real-time cycling alerts for drivers to help create a safer environment on the road.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/waze-garmin-cycling-alerts-scaled.jpg" alt="Waze cycling alerts " width="2560" height="1433" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1076660" /><br/>
Going forward, when cyclists turn on Garmin LiveTrack on their Garmin Edge bike computer or Garmin smartwatch, they can choose to show up in Waze as a real-time moving icon. <br/>
<br/>
Drivers will also see a notification when a cyclist is nearby, so they can slow down, stay aware, and share the road.<br/>
<br/>
The feature is completely opt-in, and Waze and Garmin say it is designed with privacy in mind. Drivers only see a temporary alert that a cyclist is nearby, and a cyclist's name, identity, or exact route is never shared in the app. Alerts also automatically turn off the moment a cyclist ends their ride on the Garmin device.<br/>
<br/>
